    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_b1500756d7b4a49aa466e6933c3a9bf1c87b39f24b5d5ec372e9f1e6d428322f",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The pair-correlation weighted Paley-Wiener space is first identified isometrically with a de Branges space H(E). The companion functions A and B, or the endpoint-aligned auxiliary E_beta, then supply interpolation nodes; Krein factorization and orthogonal reproducing-kernel bases turn the preserved weighted integral into an exact node sum. Interpolation can consequently construct interval majorants and minorants at those nodes while the same quadrature identities certify their optimal weighted costs.",
